  "articleBody": "A garage conversion can add incredible value and functionality to your home, but it’s definitely a project where missteps can be costly. One of the most frequent mistakes we see is failing to clearly plan the new use of the room. Without a defined purpose, you risk creating a space that doesn't truly meet your needs. Another big one is underestimating the overall cost; conversions often involve more than just cosmetic changes, with electrical, plumbing, and insulation needs adding up quickly. Ignoring permit and code requirements is a huge no-no, as this can lead to fines or even force you to tear out completed work. Always check with your local building department, especially if you're in areas like Denver or Parker. And please, avoid trying to save money by doing complex work without proper skills. Tasks like structural modifications, significant electrical upgrades, or installing proper insulation are best left to professionals to ensure safety and compliance. When you’re ready for a reliable team, HH Remodeling LLC can help you navigate these complexities and deliver a successful conversion, serving all around the greater Denver area.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}